# Frontend environment variables (Vite)
#
# The API base is NOT configured here — it is derived from the build target
# (see src/platform/target.ts):
#
#   desktop    npm run build      -> http://127.0.0.1:8000
#               The SPA runs in a Tauri webview (origin tauri://localhost) and
#               the backend is a separate origin on loopback, so API calls
#               need an absolute base.
#
#   companion  npm run build:web  -> same origin (empty base)
#               FastAPI serves the SPA itself at /app/, so the API is the same
#               origin on every device. A bundle that hard-coded a host would
#               make a phone call its own localhost.
#
# Both production targets ignore VITE_API_URL, so the same commit produces the
# same bundle on every machine.
#
# This file is for the DEV server only: copy it to ui/.env (untracked) to point
# `npm run dev` at a backend somewhere else — a custom port, a NAS, a tunnel.
#
#   VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000
#
# Use the explicit IPv4 loopback (127.0.0.1), not `localhost`: the server binds
# IPv4 only, and `localhost` can resolve to ::1 first on macOS.

VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
